Exactly what's wrong with that plan is that it is so
easy to add XL early, and the PC is so unready for
the resultingly more difficult monsters.

That's one of NetHack's seductive traps courtesy of
the Dev Team, along with plate mail and other "it
looks good until you try it" "gifts".

The HP from potions come without the disadvantage of
making the monsters harder for you AND for your pets
at the same time.

Moreover, as a healer, you start with all three
healing potion types IDed, so you know to quaff any
random ones you find, from the beginning. This can
easily add three or four more HP by Mines Town.

