The protection racket is always an "if possible"
strategy. If I lose a pet, I play an entirely
different game, until, perhaps, I tame a new pet.

If I get cornered by monsters and my pet is off
sniffing fire hydrants somewhere, I kill the
monsters and take the XP hit rather than die.

Then I start again to play the protection racket,
but at a higher per point AC cost and lower total
protection because of the XL added between pets.

What is described, arriving at Mines Town, Sokoban's
Treasure Room, and Mines End all at XL:1, is an
_ideal_.

I'm still lousy at the last one: though I've done it
several times, as yet I don't manage it regularly.

Since some pacifists do ascend, I know its possible
to do Mines End without killing monsters, and I'm
working to add accomplishing it routinely to my
skill set.

